{"number":6,"title":"Linux: keep the window manager's title bar buttons only","state":"OPEN","draft":false,"author":"switch87","created_at":"2026-10-08T11:11:12Z","updated_at":"2026-10-14T20:44:51Z","merged_at":null,"closed_at":null,"merge_commit":null,"base_ref":"main","head_ref":"linux-window-buttons","head_commit":"945c74dc3d4563830c53088c6a6b25e6626f457f","closes":[],"paths":["frontend/apps/artcraft/app/src/components/signaled/TopBar/TopBar.tsx"],"paths_total":1,"body":"ArtCraft-X builds and runs on Linux (I built an AppImage with `npx @tauri-apps/cli@2 build --bundles appimage` on Gentoo, KDE Plasma 6.7 on Wayland, WebKitGTK 2.54), but it showed two sets of window buttons: the window manager's and the app's own.\n\nThe custom minimize/maximize/close buttons in `TopBar.tsx` were drawn on every platform except macOS, but only Windows hides the native title bar (`decorations(false)` in `setup_main_window.rs`, which notes that `decorations(false)` breaks resizing on Linux). They are now drawn only on Windows; Linux keeps its window manager's buttons. Same fix as storytold/artcraft#1994.\n\nTested: after the change the AppImage starts with a single set of buttons and the prompt workspace works. Not tested on Windows or macOS; on those platforms the condition evaluates exactly as before."}
{"number":7,"title":"Linux installers: fix beforeBuildCommand, add desktop entry and icons","state":"OPEN","draft":false,"author":"a904guy","created_at":"2026-10-08T22:01:18Z","updated_at":"2026-10-08T22:01:18Z","merged_at":null,"closed_at":null,"merge_commit":null,"base_ref":"main","head_ref":"linux-installers","head_commit":"690b28eb673bed7020e6e79a67fd0d9edbac8514","closes":[],"paths":["crates/artcraftx/icons/256x256.png","crates/artcraftx/linux/artcraftx.desktop","crates/artcraftx/tauri.conf.json"],"paths_total":3,"body":"ArtCraft-X on Linux: fix the production build and add a proper desktop entry and icons\n\ncargo tauri build currently fails before it compiles anything, because the build command has a typo. This PR fixes that and adds the packaging metadata needed for a usable Linux .deb.\n\nChanges\n\n- Fix beforeBuildCommand (tauri.conf.json): it was npx run artcraft:build, which is missing nx, so every production build stopped at the frontend step. It's now npx nx run artcraft:build, matching ArtCraft.\n- Bundle metadata: adds category, short and long descriptions, publisher, homepage and the deb section, so the desktop entry gets Categories=Graphics and a Comment.\n- Desktop entry template (crates/artcraftx/linux/artcraftx.desktop): used for .deb and .rpm. It adds GenericName, Keywords, TryExec, StartupNotify and StartupWMClass on top of Tauri's defaults, so the app shows up in launcher searches and the dock can match the window to its icon.\n- 256 px icon: 128x128@2x.png was being installed into hicolor/256x256@2/, a folder for 512 px images at 2× scale. This adds a real icons/256x256.png, and the package now ships correct 32, 64, 128, 256 and 512 px icons.\n\nTested\n\nOn Ubuntu 26.04 (GNOME on Wayland, NVIDIA RTX 4090):\n\n- cargo tauri build --bundles deb,appimage builds both packages.\n- sudo apt install ./ArtCraftX_0.0.1_amd64.deb installs cleanly.\n- The installed .desktop file passes desktop-file-validate.\n- All icons are in the hicolor icon cache at the correct sizes.\n- ArtCraft-X launches from the app launcher and renders its UI."}
{"number":9,"title":"Send Fal's JSON content type once","state":"OPEN","draft":false,"author":"api-haus","created_at":"2026-10-12T18:47:09Z","updated_at":"2026-10-19T11:33:41Z","merged_at":null,"closed_at":null,"merge_commit":null,"base_ref":"main","head_ref":"fix/fal-duplicate-content-type","head_commit":"1e5e653bf6c16aaada48b795c242eec8e8adaf63","closes":[],"paths":["crates/api_clients/fal_client/src/requests/core_api/fal_request.rs"],"paths_total":1,"body":"`FalRequest` calls `.json(&self.params)` and then `.header(\"Content-Type\", \"application/json\")`. reqwest's `.json()` already sets the header and `.header()` appends, so the request carries two `Content-Type` headers. Fal's queue accepts it, but the job runs with a body it treats as binary, and the response URL returns:\n\n```\n422 {\"detail\":[{\"type\":\"model_attributes_type\",\"loc\":[\"body\"],\"msg\":\"Input should be a valid dictionary or object to extract fields from\",\"input\":\"<binary 95 bytes>\"}]}\n```\n\nReproduced with curl against `fal-ai/flux/schnell`: one header returns the image, two return the 422 above. With this change `flux_1_schnell` through the router enqueues, completes and downloads.\n\nAlso replaces the `println!` of the queue response with `info!`, per the workspace style."}
{"number":10,"title":"ci: configure Dependabot for Cargo and GitHub Actions","state":"CLOSED","draft":false,"author":"dylanmtaylor","created_at":"2026-10-18T17:09:28Z","updated_at":"2026-10-18T17:53:18Z","merged_at":null,"closed_at":"2026-10-18T17:53:18Z","merge_commit":null,"base_ref":"main","head_ref":"ci/configure-dependabot","head_commit":"b4bb3717dce0b5e18ef4392c58d05c95470bad48","closes":[],"paths":[".github/dependabot.yml"],"paths_total":1,"body":"Configures Dependabot to keep Rust / Cargo dependencies and GitHub Actions workflows up to date.\n\n- Schedules daily dependency checks at 06:00 America/New_York\n- Groups Cargo updates into a single consolidated PR with `chore(deps)` prefix\n- Groups GitHub Actions updates into a single consolidated PR with `ci(deps)` prefix"}
{"number":12,"title":"Skip CodeRabbit reviews on Dependabot PRs","state":"MERGED","draft":false,"author":"echelon","created_at":"2026-10-20T15:41:00Z","updated_at":"2026-10-20T15:41:07Z","merged_at":"2026-10-20T15:41:04Z","closed_at":"2026-10-20T15:41:04Z","merge_commit":"c6b5d338303251d8bcb93ec6806b412f95127936","base_ref":"main","head_ref":"coderabbit-skip-dependabot","head_commit":"83de3c77967f986c3690b6994482c2f862c237d1","closes":[],"paths":[".coderabbit.yaml"],"paths_total":1,"body":"Adds `.coderabbit.yaml` with `reviews.auto_review.ignore_usernames: [\"dependabot[bot]\"]` so CodeRabbit stops reviewing and commenting on Dependabot PRs. Config-only change; same file is landing across the craft repos.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)"}
